<title>USA: U.S. daily aluminum output climbs in March.</title>
<headline>U.S. daily aluminum output climbs in March.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The daily rate of primary aluminum production in the United States in March rose to 9,908 tonnes compared to 9,901 tonnes in February, and 9,779 tonnes in March last year, the Aluminum Association reported.</p>
<p>The annualised rate of production in March was 3,616,373 tonnes, compared to 3,613,865 tonnes in February, and 3,579,161 tonnes in March 1996.</p>
<p>Actual output in March this year was 307,144 tonnes, bringing the first quarter total to 889,763 tonnes.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
